   "subject": "How to save multiple plots in one doc file?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div style=\"text-align:right\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\">Hi,</p></div></blockquote></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div style=\"text-align:right\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\">I created a loop to save multiple plots in a pdf file:</p></div></blockquote></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div style=\"text-align:right\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">var.names=colnames(df) </span><span lang=\"HE\" dir=\"RTL\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">PDF_filename = &quot;C:/Users/df_.pdf&quot;\r\n#opening pdf file for writing<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">pdf(file=PDF_filename)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">for (i in 2:ncol(df)){<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"> \r\nplot(df$PET_Total, df[[i]], ylab=var.names[i])<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">}</span><span lang=\"HE\" dir=\"RTL\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">dev.off() <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\">I want to do the same but save the plots in a doc file. I can I do\r\nthis?</p></div></blockquote></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div style=\"text-align:right\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\"><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr;unicode-bidi:embed\">Thanks!<u></u><u></u></p></div></blockquote></blockquote>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "D2M9IwzNCgAJ",
   "from": "Jonathan Rosenblatt",
   "author": "a305e65fa9dfb74d",
   "date": "2015-10-23T13:39:57Z",
   "subject": "Re: [Israel RUG] How to save multiple plots in one doc file?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I have no idea how to export to .DOC, but if you can export a single plot, then you can arrange all your output in a single plot, and then export it as one.<div>Look at gridExtra::grid.arrange</div><div><br><div><br></div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Oct 23, 2015 at 12:16 PM, Simon Givoli <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">giv...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;border-right:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex;padding-right:1ex\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div style=\"text-align:right\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\">Hi,</p></div></blockquote></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div style=\"text-align:right\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\"><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\">I created a loop to save multiple plots in a pdf file:</p></div></blockquote></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div style=\"text-align:right\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\"><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">var.names=colnames(df) </span><span lang=\"HE\" dir=\"RTL\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">PDF_filename = &quot;C:/Users/df_.pdf&quot;\r\n#opening pdf file for writing<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">pdf(file=PDF_filename)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">for (i in 2:ncol(df)){<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"> \r\nplot(df$PET_Total, df[[i]], ylab=var.names[i])<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">}</span><span lang=\"HE\" dir=\"RTL\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\">dev.off() <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\">I want to do the same but save the plots in a doc file. I can I do\r\nthis?</p></div></blockquote></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div style=\"text-align:right\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\"><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" dir=\"LTR\" style=\"text-align:left;direction:ltr\">Thanks!<span><font color=\"#888888\"><u></u><u></u></font></span></p></div></blockquote></blockquote></blockquote></div></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
